\par \tab The two light catapults can fire at Huge creatures. With the \endash 1 modifier for concealment, the
 light catapults have adjusted THAC0s of 15. The attack rolls are 15 and 6. The first shot hits the umber hulk, and because of the direct hit, the umber hulk gets no saving throw and suffers 3d10 points of damage from it (the goblins are still using masse
s
 of small stones). The miss scatters, using the square containing the umber hulk's head as the intended impact square. The roll is a 2, a straight overshot. The distance roll also is a 2, which places the umber hulk within the shot's area of effect in spi
te of the miss. The umber hulk has 8+8 Hit Dice and gets a saving throw vs. petrification to avoid damage; it rolls a 19, easily succeeding. Nevertheless, the direct hit convinces it to retreat below ground with its prize.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6\cgrid0 Direct Fire Engines
\par }{\fs24\cgrid0 Ballistae and
 cannons fire their projectiles in a low, flat curve. They are fairly accurate, though somewhat difficult to aim at small targets. Only light ballistae can be aimed as freely as a hand-held weapon can; larger engines can hit small targets only by aiming a
t the area containing the target.
\par \tab All targets are considered Armor Class 10. If the target is a creature (not an area containing a creature) bonuses from Dexterity and magical protections apply. The attack roll is modified as follows:
\par 
